course: dictionary
lesson: 8609
title: One word, many meanings: scrape
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Scrape is a word with several meanings. Its meaning depends on the words around it. «Chairs scraped, everybody jumped up to watch.» Here scrape is a sound. Chairs rubbing on the floor make a rough, scratching noise.
explain: «Please scrape the mud off your shoes before you come in.» Here scrape is an action: you rub something with a hard or sharp edge to take the mud away. Check the clues: mud and shoes tell you what is happening.
explain: Scrape can also be a noun, a thing that happens. «A graze scrapes off the top layer of skin.» A scrape is a small injury where your skin is rubbed raw. «The twins got into a scrape when they climbed the wall.» Here a scrape is a difficult situation. The word «into» is a clue that it is a place you can get stuck in.
fact: Scrape is a verb and a noun. As a verb it can be scrape, scrapes, scraped or scraping.
fact: «Scrape» can mean to rub something off with a hard or sharp edge, like mud from shoes.
fact: «Scrape» can mean a small injury to your skin, like a scraped knee. A scrape is also a difficult situation.
fact: «Scrape through» means to only just pass, as in «Tom scraped through his spelling test by one mark.»
fact: «Scrape together» means to gather something with difficulty, often a little money or food.
exercise: «Chairs scraped, everybody jumped up to watch.» What does scraped mean here? | *Made a rough, scratching sound as they moved | Were broken into pieces | Were carried outside | Were painted bright red
exercise: Ella fell in the playground and has a scrape on her knee. What is a scrape? | *A small injury where the skin is rubbed raw | A long journey on a bus | A loud shout | A kind of cake
exercise: «Tom scraped through his spelling test by one mark.» What does scraped through mean? | *Only just passed | Cheated and was caught | Passed with top marks | Did not sit the test
test: «Please scrape the mud off your shoes before you come in.» What does scrape off mean here? | *Rub away with a hard edge | Tie up tightly | Wash in the sea | Paint over
test: «The twins got into a scrape when they climbed the wall.» What is a scrape here? | A soft breeze | A kind of bird | Dinner | *A difficult situation
exam: «Sam had a scrape on his elbow, so he cleaned it with water.» What is a scrape here? | A pair of shoes | *A small injury to the skin | A pile of leaves | A loud noise
